# ==== T-FMT-B — the ONE keyword synonym that is CANONICALIZED, not preserved.
# PIN (Core #12 escape hatch — nothing in THIS track implements the elif
# rewrite, so there is no own-mechanism to break; the header states what the
# cell pins instead, and the RED was demonstrated during the round by
# temporarily flipping the emitter's `"elif "` literal and watching this test
# fail).
# SCOPE CLAIM: `else if` -> `elif`. The preserve family is the set of spellings
# that carry AUTHORIAL INFORMATION; `elif` and `else if` are the same construct
# with the same reading, so the pair carries none — it is the stated exception
# to the preserve rule (ledger, 2026-08-11 ELIF SUPERSESSION). This fixture is
# written in the ALREADY-CANONICAL form and must stay a fixed point: it exists
# so that a future contributor extending the verbatim chokepoint does NOT
# "helpfully" add `else if` to the preserve set.
void main():
    int x = 2
    if x == 1:
        print(1)
    elif x == 2:
        print(2)
    else:
        print(3)
